<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Decapolis</h1><p class="st-meta">1354 CE – 1679 CE · capital Haguenau</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A defensive league of ten Alsatian imperial cities, founded in 1354, that guarded their freedoms until Louis XIV absorbed them into France.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1354 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Emperor Charles IV</a> approved an alliance of ten imperial cities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>: <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-haguenau">Haguenau</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-colmar">Colmar</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-wissembourg">Wissembourg</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-selestat">Sélestat</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-obernai">Obernai</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-kaysersberg">Kaysersberg</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-rosheim">Rosheim</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-munster">Munster</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-turckheim">Turckheim</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-mulhouse">Mulhouse</a>. They promised one another aid against the nobility and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-strasbourg">Strasbourg</a>, under the protection of the imperial bailiff (Landvogt) at Haguenau.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The league had no central government; delegates met in assemblies to settle disputes, share military costs and defend each member's rights. Membership changed: <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-mulhouse">Mulhouse</a> left in 1515 to ally with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/old-swiss-confederacy">Old Swiss Confederacy</a>, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-landau">Free Imperial City of Landau</a> took its place in 1521. The members divided over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-colmar">Colmar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landau">Landau</a> becoming Protestant while others stayed Catholic.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> in 1648 transferred the imperial bailiwick to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, whose kings treated it as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> forced the cities to submit and had their walls razed in 1673, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaties-of-nijmegen">Treaty of Nijmegen</a> of 1679 confirmed their annexation to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/decapolis.jpg" alt="Decapolis" width="320" height="462"><figcaption>Image: Nichalp · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The-Decapolis-map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1354 CE – 1679 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Haguenau</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Alsatian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Alsatian Decapolis, Zehnstädtebund</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1516&amp;focus=decapolis" aria-label="Decapolis on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5598 989 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Decapolis lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path cl